tialias`/`gtk-xft-rgba` before the webview is built, plan §2 #60), `commands.rs` (commands ≤ 15 lines delegating to `session` through `Merge::session`, or to `merge.rs`; `abort_merge`, `abort_operation` and a finished `continue_operation` destroy the window, which ends the event loop without a close request, so the page asks nothing; the two async commands take the window and read the state from it, since tauri's check of an async command with a borrowed argument expands to an `unreachable!`; `with_session` manages `Mutex<Merge>`, calls `servers::manage` for the host, sets the invoke handler and registers the app's one page-load hook: a page that starts loading calls `servers::stop_runs_on_page_start`; Tauri keeps only the last `on_page_load`, so no other place registers one), `servers.rs` (`manage`: builds and manages the `HostState` (`Mutex<Host>`) for the session's repository, nothing else; `stop_runs_on_page_start`: on `PageLoadEvent::Started` stops every run of the page before it (`Host::stop_every`), since a reloaded page's channels still take events; the six language server commands, plan §2 #70: `servers_context`, `start_server` — a small thread forwards the run's events into its Tauri `Channel` and, when a send fails, drops them so the run stops itself —, `send_to_server`, `stop_server`, `find_program`, `project_files`), `settings.rs` (`Places` and the eight settings commands; `set_server_answer` and `set_server_switch` (a found server switched off or on, plan §2 #83) key their change by the host's root, and a root that is not UTF-8 only reads), `ipc_error.rs` (`IpcError`, mapped from `yamt_session::Error` — git's refusal of a Continue is `Git` with git's own text —, plus `MergeAborted`, `GitRunning`, `MergeFinished`), `frontend_log.rs` (`LogEntry` → `tracing`, target `frontend`), `mock_window.rs` (tests only: a conflict or operation repository opened in a mock-runtime window, `invoke` a command by name, `invoke_on` from another thread; used by the command 